# Dataset Description

The dataset contains information about 571 films nominated for or awarded 
the Oscar for Best Picture in the period from 1927 to 2020. The data was 
collected from publicly available sources (IMDb, Rotten Tomatoes) and includes 
film characteristics, audience and critic ratings, and award information.

The dataset consists of **571 observations** and **20 variables**.

```{r}
oscars <- read.csv("oscars_dataset.csv", sep = ";", 
                   na.strings = c("", "NA", "Unknown"), encoding = "UTF-8")
glimpse(oscars)
```
## Key Variables

The dataset contains variables divided into several categories:

**Basic information:** Film (title), Oscar.Year (year of award), Award (Winner/Nominee)

**Film characteristics:** Year.of.Release, Movie.Time (duration in minutes), Main.Genre, Content.Rating (age classification)

**Ratings:** IMDB.Rating (1-10), IMDB.Votes, Tomatometer.Rating (critics, 0-100), Audience.Rating (audience, 0-100)


# Data Preparation for Analysis
Let's convert the data to the appropriate type:
```{r}
oscars$Award <- factor(oscars$Award,
                       levels = c("Nominee", "Winner"))
oscars$Main.Genre <- factor(oscars$Main.Genre)
oscars$Subgenre <- factor(oscars$Subgenre)
oscars$Content.Rating <- factor(oscars$Content.Rating)
oscars$Movie.Genre <- factor(oscars$Movie.Genre)
oscars$Year.of.Release <- as.numeric(oscars$Year.of.Release)
oscars$Movie.Time <- as.numeric(oscars$Movie.Time)
oscars$IMDB.Rating <- as.numeric(oscars$IMDB.Rating)
oscars$IMDB.Votes <- as.numeric(gsub(",", "", oscars$IMDB.Votes))
oscars$Tomatometer.Rating <- as.numeric(oscars$Tomatometer.Rating)
oscars$Tomatometer.Count <- as.numeric(oscars$Tomatometer.Count)
oscars$Audience.Rating <- as.numeric(oscars$Audience.Rating)
oscars$Audience.Count <- as.numeric(oscars$Audience.Count)
oscars$Original.Release.Date <- as.Date(oscars$Original.Release.Date)
```

**Data type conversion:**  
Categorical variables (`Award`, `Main.Genre`, `Content.Rating` etc.) were converted to factors, while numeric variables (`Year.of.Release`, `Movie.Time`, rating variables) were converted to numeric format.


**Data filtering:**  
Let's see how many missing values there are: 
```{r}
nasum <- colSums(is.na(oscars))
kable(nasum[nasum > 0], col.names = "Number of NA values")
```
We currently do not remove records with NA values as this would mean significant data loss, so we keep them in the dataset for now.


